.TH DEMAKE\-ARRANGE 1 "" "" "Convert any track into hardware\-compliant chip music"
.SH NAME
demake-arrange \- Convert any track into hardware\-compliant chip music
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdemake arrange\fR [\fIoptions\fR] [\fIinput\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Convert any track into hardware\-compliant chip music.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-console\fR \fI<id>\fR
Target console id or alias (e.g. gb, nes, sms). [required]
.TP
\fB\-\-preview\fR \fI<file>\fR
Also write a playable audio file of the exact result.
.TP
\fB\-\-preview-format\fR \fIvalue\fR
Preview encoding. WAV and FLAC are sample\-exact; lossy formats land with their encoders. (default: wav)
.TP
\fB\-\-output-stage\fR \fIvalue\fR
Raw chip output, or the console's analog stage simulated. (default: raw)
.TP
\fB\-\-effort\fR \fIvalue\fR
Search budget: one candidate, a pruned portfolio, or the full one. (default: default)
.TP
\fB\-\-strategy\fR \fIauto|<name>|list\fR
Tournament control: auto (default), a candidate name, or list. (default: auto)
.TP
\fB\-\-strict\fR
Fail rather than degrade.
.TP
\fB\-\-emit-manifest\fR \fI[path]\fR
Also write the sidecar JSON: channel plan, timing, budgets, provenance.
.TP
\fB\-\-bpm\fR \fI<n>\fR
Override the detected tempo.
.TP
\fB\-\-tempo\fR \fIvalue\fR
Hold the source tempo, or let the bounded tempo grade pick a cheaper grid. (default: exact)
.TP
\fB\-\-role\fR \fI<part>=<role>\fR
Override a part's role (percussion|bass|lead|harmony|pad|arp|fx); repeatable.
.TP
\fB\-\-drop\fR \fI<part>\fR
Exclude a part outright; repeatable.
.TP
\fB\-\-channels\fR \fI<n>\fR
Cap the channels used; the rest stay silent.
.TP
\fB\-\-reserve\fR \fI<channel>\fR
Keep a channel free for sound effects; repeatable.
.TP
\fB\-\-title\fR \fI<text>\fR
Track title, stored in the file.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<file>\fR
Write the artifact to <file> (default: stdout when piped).
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit a single JSON object on stdout (product goes to \-o).
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase diagnostic detail (repeatable).
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress warnings.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
Overwrite an existing output file.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
demake arrange song.mid \-c gb \-o song.vgm \-\-preview song.wav
.br
chip music, plus audio that is exactly what the cartridge plays
.PP
demake arrange track.mid \-c nes \-\-bpm 128 \-\-role 3=bass
.br
pin the tempo, correct a role
.PP
demake arrange song.mid \-c sms \-\-json
.br
channel plan, timing, drops, scoreboard
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBdemake\fR(1)
